    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "38 Saint Anne’s is a well-positioned two-bedroom terraced home situated within a mature and established setting in the heart of Kimmage. The property benefits from a practical and well-balanced layout, with generous room proportions that provide comfortable living and bedroom accommodation.\r\n\r\nInternally, the property is bright and functional throughout, comprising a welcoming living room to the front with open fireplace, and a kitchen/dining area to the rear with direct access to the garden. Upstairs, there are two spacious double bedrooms, both with built-in storage, along with a main bathroom. While the property would benefit from some modernisation, it offers a solid and straightforward opportunity for a buyer to upgrade and tailor the interior to their own specification.\r\n\r\nExternally, the property enjoys a private rear garden, providing useful outdoor space for everyday use or further enhancement. To the front, there is off-street parking. The surrounding environment is quiet and settled, contributing to a strong sense of stability and long-term appeal within the development.\r\n\r\nSaint Anne’s is a well-regarded and convenient location, within walking distance of a wide range of local amenities including shops, cafés and services along Kimmage Road Lower and Sundrive Road. The nearby villages of Harold’s Cross, Terenure, Rathgar and Crumlin further enhance the offering, providing an excellent selection of retail, dining and leisure options.\r\n\r\nThe area is also well served by a number of established primary and secondary schools, while nearby parks such as Eamonn Ceannt Park, Bushy Park and Sundrive Park offer valuable green space and recreational facilities. Public transport is readily available, with multiple Dublin Bus routes providing direct access to the city centre. The M50 road network is easily accessible, and the Red Line Luas at Rialto is within a short commute, ensuring strong connectivity across Dublin.\r\n\r\nAccommodation\r\nGround Floor\r\nEntrance Hallway – 0.9m x 1.3m\r\nLiving Room – 3.7m x 4.3m - Bright reception room with open fireplace and stairs to first floor\r\nKitchen / Dining Room – 3.7m x 2.7m - Fitted units, door to rear garden\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\nLanding / Hallway – 0.8m x 2.4m\r\nBedroom 1 (Front) – 3.8m x 2.6m - Built-in wardrobe\r\nBedroom 2 (Rear) – 3.8m x 2.6m - Built-in wardrobe\r\nBathroom – 2.8m x 1.5m - Bath with shower, WHB and WC\r\nHot Press / Storage\r\n\r\nLocal area\r\nSchools: Presentation, Harold's Cross NS, Scoil Mológa, Rosary College, Terenure College, Stratford College, Our Lady’s, and many more nearby\r\nBus routes (within 10 mins): 9, 15a, S4, 54A and 74  \r\n\r\nProperty features\r\nc. 62 sq. m. (667 sq. ft.)\r\nC2 BER rating\r\nGFCH\r\nDriveway parking\r\nYear of construction: 1983\r\n\r\nFeatures\r\nQuiet and mature residential location\r\nTwo generous double bedrooms\r\nPrivate rear garden with patio and lawn\r\nOff-street parking to front\r\nGas-fired central heating\r\nDouble glazed windows\r\nExcellent potential to upgrade and add value"
      },
